Z||000000||otis||03-02-2001||02:30 PM||||Okay here goes. I start my 86GT in the morning and drive 5 min. and the temp light comes on but the motor does not feel hot. I let the motor continue to run until the stat opens and the cooling fan starts. At this point the temp light goes out. I removed the stat and checked for temp light the next morning. This time no temp light throughout my 30 min drive to work. Next I tried three different stats. Got the same result as original set of parameters. Is it just air or is the block cracked,exhaust leak into the water jacket? Thanks<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||otis||03-02-2001||02:33 PM||||P.S.<BR>Thanks for the brake research. I along with many others have done the Grand Am upgrade based on the word of other Fiero techies. It is good to have people like you that are concerned with safety as a number one priority.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||03-02-2001||11:31 PM||||there are 2 things you could try.<P>1. hook a scanner to the ALDL and see what the ECM says the engine temperature is.<P>2. simply replace the sender. the light and the gauge use the same sender. If the gauge says it's ok and the light comes on then maybe that the sender is bats.<P>the scanner would tell you for sure if air trapping is a problem. The ECM would also report hot. <P>If you suspect air trapping then check the heater core for seeping. you'll want to take off the cover and actually see if there is evidence of a leak. a slow leak can be contained in the heater housing. you'll also need to check the rest of the system. you also want to make sure you have the right radiator cap.<P>thanks for the comment on brake upgrades. there is more info comming for that article. Some present sections are being reworked.<P>Did you do all 4 wheels or just the front? Do you like it?||||reg||1
Z||000003||otis||03-03-2001||12:19 AM||||I only did the front due to safety inspection laws requiring a rear parking brake on all cars that can stop a vehicle going 20 mph. ||||reg||1
